  "post": {
    "caption": "The first X ray showed a ring. In November 1895, Wilhelm Roentgen discovered a new kind of ray and called it X for the unknown. In December he laid his wife Anna Bertha's hand over a photographic plate. The picture showed the bones of her hand, with a dark band around one finger, her wedding ring. He mailed copies of the picture to physicists across Europe. In 1901, Roentgen won the very first Nobel Prize in Physics.",
